## 2026-09-16 — 22:34 IST

### Investigated and fixed "Unable to publish this listing" error

Why: Admin reported a 500-level error dialog every time they attempted to publish a single property from the property description composer. The generic message "We could not complete this request right now" was shown.

Investigation path:
- `frontend-web/src/components/MasterAdminDashboard.tsx` — confirmed pre-flight validation passes for a valid prompt; error originates from `createPropertyFromParsed` → `POST /api/v1/properties/create-from-parsed`.
- `frontend-web/src/services/apiError.ts` — confirmed the ≥500 status bucket maps to the generic customer-safe message.
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/controller/PropertyController.java` — traced execution: listing save succeeds then `recordPublishedParserReview` is called.
- PostgreSQL: `\dt parser*` returned zero rows — the three new tables did not exist.

Root cause 1 — Missing database tables:
- The Spring Boot backend was running since 12:47 IST (PID 77667).
- ChatGPT added `ParserTrainingExample`, `ParserFieldReview`, and `ParserModelVersion` entities at 19:38 IST — after the last startup.
- `ddl-auto: update` only creates tables at startup. The new entities were never seen, so `parser_training_examples`, `parser_field_reviews`, and `parser_model_versions` were never created.
- Every publish attempt threw a Hibernate `SQLGrammarException` inside the `@Transactional` boundary, rolling back the listing save and returning HTTP 500.

Root cause 2 — `@Autowired` missing on `ParserModelRegistryService`:
- The class has two constructors: a public one for Spring injection (with `@Value`) and a package-private one for unit tests.
- Spring 6 requires `@Autowired` on the intended constructor when multiple constructors exist. Without it, Spring attempts to find a no-args default constructor and throws `BeanInstantiationException` at startup.

Where changed:
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/service/ParserModelRegistryService.java`

What changed:
- Added `@Autowired` to the public production constructor and the corresponding `import` statement.
- Killed the stale backend process and restarted. Hibernate auto-created all three missing tables on startup.

Verification:
- `mvn clean compile` passed with 0 errors.
- Backend started in 3.065 seconds: `Started PathomeSpacesApplication`.
- `psql \dt parser*` confirmed all three tables created: `parser_training_examples`, `parser_field_reviews`, `parser_model_versions`.
- The property publish flow should now work end-to-end.

Commit status:
- Not committed. The `ParserModelRegistryService.java` fix should be included in the next commit. The `backend/src/main/resources/application.yml` must NOT be committed (contains local secrets).

